This project implements the algorithms described in RFC 6330.
RFC 6330 authors: M. Luby, A. Shokrollahi, M. Watson, T. Stockhammer, L. Minder.
Standard: https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6330.html

The fixed Rand tables and systematic parameter table in standard_tables.mbt,
and the HDPC recurrence in matrix.mbt, are adapted from cberner/raptorq,
by Christopher Berner and contributors, licensed under Apache-2.0.
Reference revision: 73e4e97b0e4d9048c49d195903e440662ef1660b
Source: https://github.com/cberner/raptorq
Changes: MoonBit translation, complete 477-row parameter table, sparse inactivation and dense/online
GF(256) elimination, legacy bounded APIs, full OTI/sub-block layout and strict packet parsing.
The new inactivation solver is independently implemented in MoonBit.
The complete Apache-2.0 license is provided in LICENSE.

reference_vectors_test.mbt and standard_layout_vectors_test.mbt are generated from the independently executed
Rust raptorq 2.0.0 Python binding. It is reference test data, not handwritten
MoonBit algorithm implementation. Python helpers implement framing and
experiment orchestration, including independent RFC sub-block layout checks;
they are not runtime codec dependencies.

Published comparison libraries, fetched by Moon, are not vendored:
